{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_25\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 25</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Similar_Triangles)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Similar Triangles)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Geometrical)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Geometrical)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Analytical)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Analytical)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Trig_+_coordinate_geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Trig + coordinate geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_25\">Problem 25</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 25\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As shown in the figure below, in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9e702326a58a2848df8758e667ae40abdbfb150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C = 90^\\circ$\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e5c76d295875eedec88e18c0a7ef4ab99266460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/f/3bf318adbc664ea1b3a7b469be11de66bce0de67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />; in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e08af8f3acc34996e3cba566dc970b7ed496ba4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADB$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/9/51994cfbd179549b6c8744eedeb78bab08a04a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle D = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4ca7c070aae6f493adce48a3f6220f8e44a68dbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = BD$\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" />. Line segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. What is the distance from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/7/d9784b7f287476ae8fe839e0b6e7a62d2ff4c0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2\\frac{1}{7}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2\\frac{1}{6}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\frac{1}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2\\frac{1}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2\\frac{2}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"416\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Screenshot_2026-08-11_160829.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/09/Screenshot_2026-08-11_160829.png/350px-Screenshot_2026-08-11_160829.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"350\" height=\"227\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/09/Screenshot_2026-08-11_160829.png/525px-Screenshot_2026-08-11_160829.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/09/Screenshot_2026-08-11_160829.png/700px-Screenshot_2026-08-11_160829.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Similar_Triangles.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Similar_Triangles)\">Solution 1 (Similar Triangles)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Similar Triangles)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the Pythagorean theorem on right <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/8/d88d3b225d4dcf1a78380f5c98940f6107e3deca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/4734af219cda9b1b8d2a209cd0a115bde1cc6935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AGC \\sim \\triangle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />, the scale factor yields:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/c/94c9e8384a718e5912f3f770bf1bce9a12de2b65.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CG = \\frac{AC \\cdot BC}{AB} = \\frac{12}{5}, \\quad AG = \\frac{AC^2}{AB} = \\frac{16}{5}\\]\" width=\"333\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/9/6c938d73e4e66dc6364e05e6d401b3ea238b3437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF = h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/d/15d5cc5c4713d60242c1b875f93e4f2cbde4a9bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AFE \\sim \\triangle AGC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />, the heights scale proportionally along the base:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/7220bc3450b8836360f844f2eb212521daa7ce0b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{AF}{AG} = \\frac{EF}{CG} \\implies AF = \\frac{16/5}{12/5}h = \\frac{4}{3}h\\]\" width=\"286\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e08af8f3acc34996e3cba566dc970b7ed496ba4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADB$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is an isosceles right triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/baf2fb7d3578f7be6b9b2fe38b6aa6be249d9e03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EBF = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />, making right <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae91ce43214ef7cd53d4ef57350933c86fa19909.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EFB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> isosceles with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/d/98d252f760ba42b30983eca69e483cf1a88b44be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF = h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Summing the segments along the base gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c233e2b0bb8c03045b7b30a5d737d68149190be8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AF + BF = AB \\implies \\frac{4}{3}h + h = 5 \\implies h = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2\\frac{1}{7}}\\]\" width=\"423\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~Icosahedron0288\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Geometrical.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Geometrical)\">Solution 2 (Geometrical)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Geometrical)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By AA if the foot of the altitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ece55f9a0c8c69d74514764c04b2a52b1cf734e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91e509833ea6818ca135897b23974bd1de032be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEF \\sim ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c68647a3390418edc1c98fb7f0479ee2b839c998.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EBF \\sim ADB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" /> by AA. Hence, the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/c/58cf2c01b32821ad23584e33cc96ba86963d7961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEF$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> has lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/9/0798e316301c45227930e369014807d5bd24baa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3k, 4k,5k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />, and the other triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea90e6937e1190a3bcca66ef907234b61b3fac6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EBF$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> has lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c64fb1aa3b69d10d6025ee0e91800f20caa179d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3k, 3k, 3k\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"23\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/f/d0fa3f5bb9e976ea62a1ae2210a1ce31f3ef8667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4k+3k = 5 \\implies k = \\frac{5}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"192\" height=\"38\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/ada52f3bd63d78b81b5a793b17d8e937c05f829d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{7} = \\boxed{2 \\frac{1}{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"82\" height=\"49\" /> is the length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Analytical.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Analytical)\">Solution 3 (Analytical)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Analytical)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/e/97ef5a3766e3fde52d0b34cb7748c24585b41c2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/7/fe73224b0990fae9451993379a4033910db26458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(5,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/9/519db5b67e558e44a3c1f5aaf8239969c263bc68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D(\\frac{5}{2}, \\frac{5}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" />. One see's that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/6/ae634d2bc49246c30b5fd7e453b62a6513a12226.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 4, BC = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />, hence by distance formulae, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/5/0356cad6171d9889282696007659bfaa7eedadd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(\\frac{16}{5}, \\frac{12}{5})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"38\" /> (negate the negative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> value as both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lie on the same side). The intersection of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/6/7369e5b7c374561f2e25ba8dee4ca375150b230a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(\\frac{20}{7}, \\frac{15}{7})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"38\" />. which implies the shortest distance is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/9/1997c7fd43697b373b3c71166bb8e145b3b27a1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{2 \\frac{1}{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"35\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Trig_.2B_coordinate_geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Trig_+_coordinate_geometry)\">Solution 4 (Trig + coordinate geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Trig + coordinate geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/8/d88d3b225d4dcf1a78380f5c98940f6107e3deca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, by the Pythagorean theorem. We also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/9494281ca98ffed9549ad092f33740b7b1bb0b6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4ca7c070aae6f493adce48a3f6220f8e44a68dbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = BD$\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is an isosceles right-angle triangle.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the origin <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b86f54134d69cad8793688a431aa907aaf2698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af222f06d92e6f05ee0014f0f97f122b319a6bc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B (5, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Reflecting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> along side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, the new point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/5/4b5e1d092e08398ad9f565e6e9f484796a8ccc0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Hence, we now know that line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> has equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/ead9786c672d768b0c11b0272acaca374cc7cdab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -x + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a7207c14fb9e5ed8cf25126a19e64eebcb14109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />. Then, we have the following:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/1/361f896ea279001119ca23bd73979a32059afa38.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(\\alpha) = \\frac{3}{5}\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/8/7a8c795320895ae47d904488c8b8b76d76a5fd9d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(\\alpha) = \\frac{4}{5}\\]\" width=\"85\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Since point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is at a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e5c76d295875eedec88e18c0a7ef4ab99266460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d72682f026b743b0660e6ae8ceaf83f340ad816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A (0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> at an angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> relative to the positive x-axis (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />), we imagine that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a point on the unit circle with the center at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. By the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> would be the y-coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> would be the x-coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/a/c1afa6ea35561e1dc2add61dc68d8943f880963a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_C = AC\\cos(\\alpha) = 4 \\cdot \\frac{4}{5} = \\frac{16}{5}\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/7/aa7566ac0fced846f0e82e0c2a4085decef1673a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y_C = AC\\sin(\\alpha) = 4 \\cdot \\frac{3}{5} = \\frac{12}{5}\\]\" width=\"227\" height=\"37\" />\nSo, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/5/6e5c0674562101c0094b0f7989cc4fd557b9f613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{16}{5}, \\frac{12}{5})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Since the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d72682f026b743b0660e6ae8ceaf83f340ad816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A (0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, so we know the slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f34e5cb8a7e4b21deae419328c2b8790051b9980.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\frac{12}{5}}{\\frac{16}{5}} = \\frac{12}{5} \\cdot \\frac{5}{16} = \\frac{3}{4}\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> has equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7abaa3e645fc53a1cffe15bb69b9a14a6f9d7ac6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{3}{4}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The distance of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is the same as the y-coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, so we put the two linear equations together and solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>\\begin{cases} y= -x + 5 \\\\ y = \\frac{3}{4}x \\end{cases}\n</p><p>Equating the two expressions we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e531c2f3acfb4e7746870186c8b1622cb4f43e7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{4}x = 5 - x\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/e/6ae7dcdd587e699d468333cb8c0a47a6fa2b7ed7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3x = 20 - 4x\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af1031c44163ca0d34713d303a15c38068e66857.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7x = 20 \\implies x = \\frac{20}{7}\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> into the original equation, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e12815238b9ecadbfe5e123a787c28ca773683af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = 5 - \\frac{20}{7} = \\frac{35 - 20}{7} = \\frac{15}{7} = 2\\frac{1}{7}\\]\" width=\"265\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Hence, we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/911b4eebd6c9066354c1f04b2bdabd03d61fae33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2\\frac{1}{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~ ThePlenGuy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems\">2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems</a></li></ul>\n<p>\\\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017184200\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 538/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18721/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37402:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017184200 and revision id 291895. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}